.git
# `**/` matches any depth including none, so this also covers the context-root
# node_modules the bare form used to name alone. The nested node_modules under
# src/FastyBird/** (four present as of this commit) were never excluded --
# Docker's node_modules glob matches only the context root, not nested paths --
# and were being copied into every build. pnpm makes this worse: a symlink farm
# per workspace package, into <root>/node_modules/.pnpm.
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
vendor
var/logs
var/temp
var/tools
env
.idea
docs
